[sliver] Required copper-cover seating shoulders. The retained cover flanges need their flat inboard seats at x=-138.30; those seats extend 0.52 mm inward from the ordinary casing. Their 1 mm bearing width matches the cover's slot-edge overlap. The straight seat has 2.90 mm of normal casing stock. The short rounded-corner return measures 4.242 mm along its flagged normal in the printed mesh.
alternatives: Removing the shoulders moves the cover's seating face and loses the retained flange contact. A taper across the 1 mm bearing removes that flat contact. Extending 2.90 mm stock across the whole face changes the selected six-bead ordinary wall. The native witnesses are in cold-core/casing-integration-review.json.
